def all_unique(items):
    seen = set()
    for item in items:
        if item in seen:
            return False
        seen.add(item)
    return True
```

This function will return `True` if all items in the list are unique, and `False` otherwise. It uses a set to keep track of the items it has seen so far, and checks if each item is already in the set before adding it. If an item is already in the set, it immediately returns `False`. If it iterates over the entire list without finding any duplicates, it returns `True`.
